  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing due to **disk full on upload storage** - not permissions or database.\n\n**Root cause: filesystem holding uploads is 100% full:**\n- `POST /upload` fails with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `out.write(chunk)` (E3)\n- Same error on health probe `open(probe,\"wb\")` (E3), which explains `/health` returning `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2)\n- `/srv/lab-data` mount: `size_mb 487.2, used_mb 451.4, available_mb 0.0, use_percent 100.0` (E4)\n- Inodes only `1.7%` (E4) - rules out inode exhaustion, is capacity exhaustion\n- Root `/` only `6.8%` used (E5) - rules out host root-disk full, isolated to `/srv/lab-data` volume\n\n**Ruled out other causes:**\n- Permissions OK: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is dir `0755`, `owner 1000:1000`, `app 1000:1000`, `app_user_can_write true` (E6); parent `/srv/lab-data` same (E7)\n- Mount present and writable: `bind source /srv/lab-data -> /data rw true` (E8), app `running true, oom_killed false, exit_code 0, restart_count 0, user 1000:1000` (E8)\n- Database dependency healthy: `incidentlab-db-1 running healthy` (E1)(E9), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` (E11), events `pg_isready exit 0` + `health_status: healthy` (E10)\n- Both containers `running Up 5s / Up 11s` (E1), no crash-loop: events show only `die exit 0` from recreate + `start` (E10)\n\nSymptom `unhealthy` (E2) and `500 Internal Server Error` on upload (E3) are downstream of storage exhaustion (E4).\n",
